From 3bd0feee2a9e7101c222eb1608b98af913a11135 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 06:32:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 286: frozen trunk clears the trunk - the reading channel is
 65 params per example

--frozen-trunk, hidden, same tapes as the nohid pass that scored EVIDENCE_OK.
Result EVIDENCE_NO, worse than the unfrozen arm on every held-out number, with
the trunk not learning a single parameter. Hypothesis (a) - the trunk
memorising subject->value at lr_upper - is dead: nothing in the trunk moved and
the collapse happened anyway. What is left is (b), and the two leave-one-out
passes say it without interpretation:

                    train control (last training tape)   held out
  unknown AUC          0.986  (+7.44 sigma)               0.416  (-0.97 sigma)
  accuracy @ coverage  0.897 @ 0.690                      0.377 @ 0.757
  selective curve      1.00 / 1.00 / 1.00 at 10-50%       flat 0.43 / 0.44 / 0.49
  vs votes matched     0.897 vs 0.690                     0.414 vs 0.431

Fitting the training tape at AUC 0.986 and landing a hair below chance on a
disjoint one, with a confidence curve that has gone completely flat, is not a
misreading. It is memorisation, and the arithmetic was available before the run:
the reading path carries 512x128 = 65,536 weights against roughly a thousand
distinct training examples - 84 leave-one-out pairs per tape, twelve tapes at
tape_period 500 - which is 65 parameters per example. The features-only head
has 1,152 weights, 1.14 per example, and it is the arm that passed.
head_input_norms had already measured the same imbalance from the other side:
the reading columns carry 3.1x the total norm of the nine features.

That is a statement about capacity, not about reading. The question "does
reading carry signal" has never been asked at a size this data can pay for, so
two changes make asking it cheap:

  --read-rank R projects the reading down before the head, so the channel can
  be given 8 or 16 dimensions instead of 512. head_input_norms now reports the
  effective width, the reading path's parameter count and the estimated number
  of distinct training examples, so the ratio is in the JSON rather than in
  someone's arithmetic.

  A frozen trunk returns the same vector for the same text forever, and the
  same tape is reused for tape_period steps, so the encodes are now cached and
  cleared on resample. Exact, not approximate - and it is most of the frozen
  arm's hour, which is what made a capacity sweep unaffordable.

Next, cheapest first: --frozen-trunk --read-rank 8, then 16. A narrow reading
that beats nohid means reading carries signal; one that merely ties means it
carries none at this tape size, and the stage's verdict is that judgment lives
in the counters.

Worth stating plainly because it would be easy to over-read: nothing here
breached the separation invariant. G_arc_enc_frozen held in every arm and the
answer is still a value taken from the visible evidence, so no fact reached the
weights in the sense the invariant forbids. What reached them is a tape-specific
way of READING, which the invariant does not name - and which the held-out tape
caught anyway.

